1. assessing the spatial distribution of [ 18 F]FDG kinetic parameters in healthy brains, with particular focus on K 1 and k 3, assuming they would provide unique information;
2. evaluating differences among [ 18 F]FDG kinetic parameters in their spatial coupling with rs-fMRI measures, employing multivariable mixed-effects modeling (MEM), with the same features chosen for our SUVR model 11 to test their reproducibility and generalizability;
3. evaluating whether including CBF and CMRO2 into the fMRI-based description of [ 18 F]FDG kinetic parameters could lead to a satisfactory description of glucose metabolism in its entirety.
